# OpenBao (`openbao-openbao`)

OpenBao helps you manage, store, and distribute sensitive data like application secrets, certificates, and keys. It provides encrypted key/value secret storage backed by persistent storage, can generate dynamic, short-lived credentials for systems like AWS and SQL databases, and supports encrypt/decrypt operations without storing the data. Built-in leasing, renewal APIs, revocation, and audit-friendly behavior make it practical to rotate credentials and limit blast radius when access needs to be cut off.

With Eyevinn Open Source Cloud (OSC), you can consume OpenBao as a managed service instead of standing up and operating your own secret-management infrastructure. You get instant provisioning without having to run servers, manage storage backends, or maintain build and deployment pipelines for a large Go codebase. Because it’s part of OSC, your managed OpenBao service fits alongside your other OSC services, letting your team focus on integrating secret workflows into applications rather than keeping the platform running.

[Source](https://github.com/openbao/openbao)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "openbao-openbao"
  name       = "myopenbao"

  sensitive_parameters = {
    UnsealKey = var.unseal_key
    AdminPassword = var.admin_password
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `UnsealKey` | string | yes | Key that unseals OpenBao automatically on every start: 32 bytes as 64 hex characters, for example generated with openssl rand -hex 32. Keep a copy somewhere safe, because the stored data cannot be decrypted without this exact key, and anyone with the key and the volume can read it. Feeds BAO_STATIC_SEAL_KEY (static seal). Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `AdminPassword` | string | yes | Password for the initial OpenBao admin user, named admin. It is applied only on the very first start, when OpenBao sets itself up, so changing this option later does not change the password. Sign in to the UI with the Username method, user admin. No root token or recovery key exists, so keep the password safe and create a second admin user, or the data cannot be recovered. Feeds BAO_ADMIN_PASSWORD. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
